\end{itemize}
These differences are formally classified as \textbf{different mesh lineage / regenerated adaptive mesh}. Both lineages are strictly separated and preserved.
 
\subsection{Companion visualizer array indexing defect and mechanics fidelity}
In the 3-layer architecture, Layer~3 companion visualizer elements (CPE4/CPE3) do not solve physical equations ($\mathbf{D}^{\mathrm{UMAT}} \approx 10^{-11}\,\mathbf{I}$, $\boldsymbol{\sigma}=\mathbf{0}$); their sole purpose is to receive and display field variables via global Fortran common blocks. In subroutine \texttt{UMAT}, the common block lookup index is $\mathrm{PHYSIDX} = \mathrm{NOEL} - 2\cdot N_{\mathrm{mesh}}$, where $N_{\mathrm{mesh}}$ is passed via \texttt{*USER MATERIAL, CONSTANTS=3}. Setting $N_{\mathrm{mesh}}$ to nominal catalog values rather than actual regenerated mesh counts produced an index offset that zeroed visualizer energies on the first $2(N_{\mathrm{nominal}} - N_{\mathrm{actual}})$ companion elements.

Crucially, the primary UEL solver operates with 100\% mathematical fidelity because \texttt{*UEL PROPERTY} specifies the exact finite element count. Consequently, while the visualizer field outputs suffered index-shift omissions, the mechanical force-displacement response ($K_0$, $F_{\max}$), softening response, and external work $W_{\mathrm{ext}}$ were completely genuine. Corrected replacement runs (\texttt{A2\_adapt\_2pct\_15k\_corrected}, \texttt{A3\_adapt\_3pct\_8k\_corrected}, \texttt{A4\_adapt\_5pct\_4k\_corrected}) restored full visualizer energy integration across 100\% of elements.

